  'highlights.label': 'Features',
  'highlights.titleLead': 'Everything you need to ',
  'highlights.titleAccent': 'write by voice',
  'highlights.titleTail': '',
  'highlights.hotkey.title': 'From hotkey to finished text',
  'highlights.hotkey.desc': 'Press one hotkey, speak, done: the transcript goes to your clipboard, and with Auto-Paste (offered during setup) it lands right at your cursor in any app. Press once to start and stop, or switch on push-to-talk and hold the key like a walkie-talkie. With hold-or-tap, a short tap toggles and a longer hold records until you let go. In English, German, Spanish, Portuguese and Russian, say "new paragraph" or "new line" to break the text. Esc throws a recording away.',
  'highlights.snippets.title': 'Voice Snippets, picked at your cursor',
  'highlights.snippets.desc': 'Reusable text blocks on call: say your trigger word or press the snippet hotkey and a searchable picker opens where you type. Interactive snippets even fill multi-field templates, one field at a time.',
  'highlights.smartmode.title': 'Smart Mode: clean up, shorten, translate',
  'highlights.smartmode.desc': 'Optional presets polish your transcript before it is pasted: Cleanup, Concise, or Translate into seven languages. Runs on a local AI model on macOS and Windows, on Linux as an experimental option, or through OpenAI with your own API key. Works on older history entries too. Off by default.',
  'highlights.sidepanel.title': 'Clipboard side panel at the screen edge',
  'highlights.sidepanel.desc': 'Move to the edge of your screen to pull out recent transcripts, snippets and copied text — one click inserts them where you work. On Windows and macOS it keeps a clipboard history; on Linux it shows what you copied last.',
  'highlights.history.title': 'Searchable history, neatly organized',
  'highlights.history.desc': 'Every transcript is kept locally and is searchable. Tag, pin, archive or merge entries, re-insert them any time and export them as TXT, Markdown, JSON, CSV or DOCX. A PIN lock with auto-lock keeps the history private.',
  'highlights.privacy.title': 'Local by default, private by design',
  'highlights.privacy.desc': 'Whisper and Parakeet transcribe on your machine: no account, no cloud requirement, recordings are not kept. Audio and text only leave your device if you pick a cloud provider with your own key. Usage statistics never contain either, crash reports are scrubbed of personal data, and both can be switched off.',
  'highlights.hardware.title': 'Runs on the hardware you have',
  'highlights.hardware.desc': 'Metal on the Mac, Vulkan on Windows and Linux, or plain CPU: WhisPaste uses the GPU when it can and falls back to the processor when it cannot. Older processors without AVX2 work too. With a recent NVIDIA card, the GitHub builds for Windows and Linux can add an optional CUDA pack.',
  'highlights.notes.title': 'Notes and quick notes',
  'highlights.notes.desc': 'Keep longer thoughts in a separate notes area. An optional quick-note hotkey adds what you say straight to the note you marked as your quick note, without opening a window.',
  'highlights.vocabulary.title': 'Your words, spelled right',
  'highlights.vocabulary.desc': 'Add names and jargon as custom vocabulary, or scan a project folder for identifiers and turn them into replacements. Replacements turn trigger words into the exact text you want, and optional filler-word removal drops the "um"s. If you correct the same thing twice, WhisPaste suggests a replacement and asks before adding it.',
  'highlights.remote.title': 'Start it from scripts and tools',
  'highlights.remote.desc': 'whispaste --toggle starts or stops a recording and --cancel discards it: bind them to a desktop shortcut, a macro key or a script. They also work on Wayland, where apps cannot grab global hotkeys. whispaste --transcribe-file <wav> prints the transcript of a WAV file. An optional local API (off by default, token-protected) lets your own tools start recordings, read the latest transcript or insert snippets.',
  'highlights.access.title': 'Always within reach',
  'highlights.access.desc': 'A tray icon (in the menu bar on the Mac) starts and stops recordings, switches the microphone and opens the settings. If you like, a small floating button stays on screen as a click-to-record alternative to the hotkey, and WhisPaste can start when you log in. Both stay off until you turn them on.',
  'highlights.backup.title': 'Take your setup with you',
  'highlights.backup.desc': 'Export your settings, replacements and snippets to one file and import them on another computer. History, recordings and API keys are left out. On Windows, the GitHub release also offers a ZIP version that runs without an installer.',
  'highlights.galleryLink': 'See it in the screenshot gallery',
  'useCaseCards.label': 'Use cases',
  'useCaseCards.more': 'See examples',
  'useCaseCards.titleLead': 'For code, study and ',
  'useCaseCards.titleAccent': 'everyday writing',
  'useCaseCards.titleTail': '',
  'useCaseCards.developer.title': 'Developers',
  'useCaseCards.developer.desc': 'Write review comments, commit messages and issue replies by voice while you keep the code in view.',
  'useCaseCards.developer.ariaLabel': 'Examples of WhisPaste for developers',
  'useCaseCards.students.title': 'Students and researchers',
  'useCaseCards.students.desc': 'Capture notes, excerpts and first drafts by voice in Word, Obsidian or your editor while the source stays in front of you.',
  'useCaseCards.students.ariaLabel': 'Examples of WhisPaste for students and researchers',
  'useCaseCards.everyday.title': 'Everyday writing',
  'useCaseCards.everyday.desc': 'Answer emails and chats or jot down a quick note without opening another tool or moving away from the current app.',
  'useCaseCards.everyday.ariaLabel': 'Examples of WhisPaste for everyday writing',
  'engines.label': 'LOCAL ENGINES',
  'engines.title': 'Two local engines for different needs',
  'engines.desc': 'Whisper covers more languages and can use a GPU. Parakeet supports fewer languages but is much faster on a CPU. You can switch between them at any time.',
  'engines.whisper.name': 'Whisper',
